# Web quality standards

When editing pages, components, styles, tokens, hero/media, marketing copy, or anything affecting Lighthouse, SEO, or accessibility, read and follow the project skill:

`.cursor/skills/web-quality-standards/SKILL.md`

**Keep the skill current:** when fixing a new audit/quality finding, update that skill (and this short list if it is a non-negotiable) in the same PR.

Non-negotiables (details in the skill):

- Keep brand coral at `#c0392b` (or deeper) so text/eyebrows pass WCAG AA on cream and white — never restore `#f26b5e` for those uses.
- No bare repeated “Learn more” / “Saber más” link text; include the destination topic in the anchor.
- Homepage LCP must be the prioritized hero `<img>` (`fetchpriority="high"`, not lazy). Do not use `video[poster]` over that image. Preload the same format `<picture>` selects (AVIF today).
- Zaraz `/cdn-cgi/zaraz/s.js` needs a browser `Cache-Control` via a Cloudflare Response Header Transform (not `public/_headers`). Zone `41a145bf2688a227f9e321a31055fe19` is in deploy; see README / `npm run cf:zaraz-cache`.
- Blog posts ship full EN + ES bodies (`src/content/blog/<slug>.md` and `src/content/blog/es/<slug>.md`) — never English-only content under `/es/blog/`.
- Non-essential cookies/trackers (analytics) require prior consent — do not load them before Accept; keep Consent Mode defaults denied.
- Canonical URLs use trailing slashes; `/privacy`, `/es/privacy`, and legacy `.html` URLs must 301 (not 307) to the slashed forms. Sitemap hreflang must include `x-default`.
- Marketing copy: industry-page specificity is the voice model — no service-overview SEO-echo third paragraphs; no “theater/teatro / slide deck / not another demo” denial stack; engineer-reply trust line once per surface. ES user-facing copy is Colombian Spanish.